he king to move and likely winning the exchange (rook for knight) as the knight will fork the king and rook on h1.\n\nReason: Nf2+ is a forcing check that puts White's king in immediate danger. After the king moves (likely Kf1 or Ke2), I can capture the rook on h1 with Nxh1, winning significant material (rook for knight). This is a tactical blow that gives Black a decisive material advantage.\n\nAnswer: N: g4-f2"}
