: **N: e4-d2+** is clearly the best move. It gives check, which forces White's king to move (likely Kf1 or Ke2 since castling would be illegal). This accomplishes multiple objectives: it disrupts White's king safety, prevents castling, and my knight on d2 would attack important squares and potentially fork pieces. After White moves the king, I can continue developing with tempo while White's king is exposed in the center.\n\nAnswer: N: e4-d2"}
