\n1 |RWF0|    |BWF0|    |KWF0|BWF0|    |RWF0| 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: b7-b5, N: b8-c6, N: b8-d7, P: c7-c6, B: c8-d7, Q: d4-a4, K: e8-d8, K: e8-e7]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: I'm playing as Black in a mid-game position. My queen is actively placed on d4, which is a strong central square. White's king is on e1 and appears vulnerable - it has moved (KWF0 shows it hasn't castled yet). White's queen is somewhat out of play on a4. I notice that White's king position looks exposed with limited defensive pieces nearby.\n\nEvaluation: Let me consider the most promising moves:\n\n1. **Q: d4-a4** - This would trade queens, simplifying the position. However, this removes my most powerful attacking piece when White's king looks vulnerable.\n\n2. **K: e8-d8 or K: e8-e7** - These king moves improve safety but are passive and don't create threats.\n\n3. **N: b8-c6** - Develops the knight to a good central square, but doesn't create immediate threats.\n\n4. **B: c8-d7** - Develops the bishop but blocks potential knight development to d7.\n\n5. **N: b8-d7** - Develops the knight, preparing to potentially reroute it to more active squares.\n\nLooking at the position more carefully, my queen on d4 is excellently placed in the center, controlling key squares and putting pressure on White's position. The most concerning issue is that my king hasn't castled yet and White's pieces could potentially create threats.\n\nReason: I'll play **N: b8-c6** because it:\n- Develops a piece actively to a strong central square\n- Supports my centralized queen\n- Prepares potential future tactics\n- Doesn't weaken my position\n- Keeps all my attacking options open while improving piece coordination\n\nAnswer: N: b8-c6"}
