ld attack along the diagonal towards e1... wait, that's not a diagonal. Let me reconsider - from g1, the queen attacks the first rank and diagonals. The king is on e1, so this would indeed be check along the first rank!\n\nReason: Q: d4-g1 delivers check to White's king on e1. This forces White to respond to the check immediately, giving me the initiative. White's options would be limited - the king must move (likely Kd2 or Kf1), or a piece must block. This tactical blow exploits White's uncastled king position and puts maximum pressure on White's position.\n\nAnswer: Q: d4-g1"}
