vating the c8 Bishop.\n\nReason: The position calls for active piece development with threats. B: c8-h3 is the strongest move because it:\n- Develops my dark-squared Bishop with a direct threat to White's Knight on h2\n- Forces White to respond to the threat\n- Places my Bishop on an aggressive diagonal\n- Improves my piece coordination\n- Is more forcing than quiet developmental moves\n\nAnswer: B: c8-h3"}
