d4 (QWF1), then P: e5-d4 would capture it! This would be an enormous material gain (9 points).\n\nReason: Capturing the White Queen with P: e5-d4 wins massive material (a Queen for a Pawn). This is by far the strongest move available. Even though my King is unsafe in the center, winning the Queen provides such a decisive material advantage that it outweighs other positional considerations. After capturing the Queen, I'll have a winning advantage and can address King safety on the next move.\n\nAnswer: P: e5-d4"}
