tion is clearly the critical move here. Between promoting on d1 or c1, both create a queen, but c1 captures the bishop (winning extra material immediately), while d1 is more centralized. However, capturing on c1 wins the bishop for free while still promoting.\n\nReason: Promoting the pawn to a queen by capturing the bishop on c1 accomplishes two things: (1) I gain a powerful queen in White's back rank, and (2) I immediately win White's bishop. This gives me overwhelming material advantage (Queen + extra bishop) that should lead to a winning position. This is much stronger than any other move.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-c1-q"}
