ms less forcing.\n\nThe critical factor is that White's knight on f1 is undefended and capturing it would be with check (since the queen on f1 would attack the king on f2). This wins material decisively.\n\nReason: Capturing the knight on f1 with check is clearly the strongest move. It forces White's king to move (likely to e2, e3, or g2), wins a full knight (3 points of material), and keeps my queen actively placed to continue the attack. This is a simple tactical win that significantly improves my position and material advantage.\n\nAnswer: Q: c1-f1"}
