n e3. I should continue pressing the advantage with forcing moves (checks) to prevent White from consolidating.\n\nReason: Q: f1-e1 delivers check to the White King on e3, forcing an immediate response. This move maintains maximum pressure, keeps White on the defensive, and doesn't allow any counterplay. After the King moves, I can continue to hunt it down with my Queen while my material advantage should convert to victory. Giving check is almost always the best option when you have a dominant position - it forces the opponent to react to your threats rather than creating their own.\n\nAnswer: Q: f1-e1"}
