ishop (winning significant material - 3 points)\n- White's King must move, giving me tempo\n- After the King moves, my Queen will be centralized and active\n\nReason: Capturing the Bishop on e4 with check is a forcing move that wins material while maintaining the initiative. This is a fundamental tactical principle - when you can capture material with check, it's usually the best move. White cannot block or capture my Queen, so the King must move, and I win the Bishop cleanly.\n\nAnswer: Q: e1-e4"}
