e (K: e8-c8) is the strongest move because:\n- It addresses king safety, which is paramount\n- It connects my rooks, bringing the h8 rook into play via d8\n- My king will be relatively safe on c8\n- After castling, I can focus on activating my pieces and exploiting White's somewhat exposed king position on b1\n- This is a fundamental principle: castle early to secure the king before launching attacks\n\nAnswer: K: e8-c8"}
