t that White must deal with. White's king on b2 is awkwardly placed - it cannot capture on d2 without moving away from defending other areas. White would likely need to block with a piece or somehow stop the pawn's advance, giving me the initiative. This forcing move maximizes my winning chances by creating concrete threats rather than passive repositioning.\n\nAnswer: P: d3-d2"}
