 pawn on d2 to a queen is by far the strongest move. A queen on d1 would:\n- Give me overwhelming material superiority (two queens worth of material advantage)\n- Create immediate threats against White's exposed king on b2\n- Control key central squares\n- Essentially guarantee a win in the resulting position\n\nThere's no reason to promote to anything other than a queen in this position, as the queen is the most powerful piece and there are no tactical reasons (like avoiding stalemate) to under-promote.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d1-q"}
