y bishop on an excellent square where it:\n- Attacks the rook on c1, forcing it to move\n- Controls important squares around White's exposed king\n- Maintains pressure on White's position\n- The bishop on c2 combined with potential future pieces can create serious threats against the king trapped on a1\n\nThis move maximizes my winning chances by maintaining the initiative and keeping White's king under pressure.\n\nAnswer: B: d3-c2"}
