 threats and limiting White's king mobility. This active piece play is critical in endgames.\n\nReason: B: c2-b1 places my bishop on the first rank, maximizing pressure on White's exposed king on a2. This forces White to deal with immediate threats rather than improving their position. In this material-up endgame (I have more pieces), maintaining active piece coordination and restricting the opponent's king is the key to converting the advantage.\n\nAnswer: B: c2-b1"}
