cks the b4 pawn immediately\n- Threatens to infiltrate on b1 or b2, forcing White's rook to remain passive\n- Improves rook activity dramatically\n- White's king on a2 becomes more vulnerable to back rank threats\n- Creates immediate tactical pressure that White must address\n\nAnswer: R: h8-b8"}
