g a response\n- **B: e1-c3** - Centralizes the bishop with good control\n- **P: c7-c5** - Pawn break to activate my position\n\nReason: **B: e1-b4** is the strongest move because it directly attacks White's b4 pawn. The pawn cannot be defended easily (the king on a3 is already protecting it, but if it moves, I win the pawn). This creates immediate tactical pressure and wins material, which is decisive in an endgame.\n\nAnswer: B: e1-b4"}
