ously attacking the White king on b2 and the knight on f1. White's king must move to escape check, and then I capture the knight on f1 for free, winning significant material (a knight is worth approximately 3 pawns). This decisive material advantage should lead to a winning endgame.\n\nAnswer: B: b4-d2"}
