o support pawn advances, particularly the f and g pawns.\n\n5. **P: f7-f5** or **P: g7-g5** - Advances pawns to create threats and restrict White's pieces.\n\nReason: With a decisive material advantage, I should activate my pieces and push for a winning position. The move **B: d2-a5** is excellent because it:\n- Places the bishop on an active diagonal\n- Restricts White's king from advancing to c4 or b4\n- Maintains flexibility for my rook and king to improve\n- Keeps all my pieces coordinated\n- Prepares for eventual pawn advances while maintaining piece activity\n\nAnswer: B: d2-a5"}
